    description: "Most dragons can take many shapes; this one is limited to three. First, a solid humanoid: a pale-skinned human or something that looks human (Lemurian, Elf and the like) whose hair is white, blue or green. That shape may be as small as a cat and may not exceed the dragon''s own size. Second, a solid, scaled-down copy of the dragon, anything down to half its true size. Third, the ghost: a spectral copy of the dragon. Any altered state lasts six hours per level of experience. As a ghost it is intangible and passes through walls and solid objects, but magic and psionic energy fields stop it. It is plainly visible as a transparent, ghostly shape and cannot turn invisible in this form, though in mist, fog and water nobody sees it until it has closed to 10 feet (3 m). It runs and swims at double speed and can fly. Most weapons and attacks cannot hurt it, and in turn it can do nothing to anyone, psionics included: only in a solid body can it injure someone in the material world. After changing to ghost or back to physical it must hold that form for one full melee round (15 seconds) before changing again. HOW OFTEN, two printed statements: the species introduction (p.211) says it can become ethereal four times a day; this ability (p.213) says the switch between ghost and solid costs no P.P.E. and can be made any number of times a day, as a natural ability. Both are recorded; the G.M. rules."
  - name: "Ghost Flight"
    description: "While it is a ghost the dragon doubles its normal speed, both swimming and flying. It can climb no higher than two miles (3.2 km)."
  - name: "Slay Ghosts and Entities"
    description: "In Ghost Form it can attack other spirits - Astral Travelers, Entities and the essences of Alien Intelligences - with claws, teeth and psionic powers. An Entity it slays has its P.P.E. eaten, which restores 1D4x10 M.D.C. to the dragon; energy taken this way is no use for spell casting. None of this lets a dragon in Ghost Form injure anybody in the material world, whatever means it tries."
  - name: "Natural Weapons"
    description: "Damage varies with Supernatural P.S. A bite does punch damage +3 M.D. and a claw strike punch damage +2D6 M.D. The prehensile tail strikes like a whip for half its punch damage. A power tail strike and a power bite are not possible. It may instead use magic, psionics or a weapon. The book prints these once and does not give the hatchling smaller figures."
restrictions:
  - "Alignment: any. The species runs mostly Anarchist (35%), Miscreant (30%), Diabolic (15%) or Aberrant (10%) and is seldom good, but a hatchling can start at any alignment."
  - "Speed: 2D6+7 running; double that swimming, or in Ghost Flight."
  - "Attacks per melee: four physical attacks per melee round, or two by breath weapon. The entry prints no by-magic figure for the hatchling, and the breath weapon''s own text limits it to once per melee round."
  - "+1 on all saving throws other than Horror Factor (which is +3)."
  - "VULNERABILITIES: an ethereal Ghost Dragon shrugs off most physical attacks. What still reaches it: any weapon able to hurt ghosts and Entities; dragon slaying magic weapons, for half their usual damage to a dragon; psionic attacks, for full damage; and all other magic weapons and spells, whose damage is halved and whose duration is cut to one third. Magic for summoning spirits, ghosts and Entities, or for protection from them, keeps it back as well, though only for as long as it stays ethereal. In physical form every attack except cold damages it. To attack by magic, psionics or physical means it must be tangible for at least one full melee round, which is when it is most exposed."
  - "MAGIC: born with a full understanding of magic but knows NO spells at level one. It can learn magic, and can use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical weapons and devices. Under the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules the book points to (p.158), spells are learned by the usual means from second level - by third level the hatchling has 2D4+2 spells from levels 1-3, another 2D4+2 by fifth level from levels 3-8, and 3 new spells per level thereafter up to its own level. Two spells may be cast per melee round, and it gains +1 to spell strength at level nine. Those counts are dice-valued, which a spell schedule cannot hold, so they are recorded here."
  - "PSIONICS: a Master Psychic. Commune with Spirits, Machine Ghost, Mind Block, Sense Magic and Sense Time, plus three powers of choice from the Sensitive category. One more is selected at levels 4, 8, 12 and 16, and Empathic Transmission arrives at level 8. The level 16 pick comes from the book; this app caps a character at level 15, so it will not fire."
  - "On S.D.C. worlds a hatchling has 5D6+7 Hit Points, 2D6x10+25 S.D.C. and a Natural A.R. of 8 in place of its M.D.C."
  - "Size: 20-24 feet (6.1 to 7.3 m) from snout to rump plus 10-15 feet (3 to 4.6 m) of tail, 7-9 feet (2.1 to 2.7 m) tall and 4-6 feet (1.2 to 1.8 m) wide at the shoulders; 3-5 tons. The book prints no separate hatchling size."
  - "It covets gold, gems, magic items and ancient artifacts, and likes hunting for sunken treasure."
  - "Diet: a carrion feeder that thrives on the dead and decaying and on the Entities such places attract."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Magic Knowledge: without being taught it can work any Techno-Wizard device, recognise and use other magic weapons, read magic and use scrolls, and it recognises magic circles and enchantment at 40% +3% per level of experience. It senses ley lines and nexus points within 20 miles (32 km), and other dragons - even ones disguised by metamorphosis - on sight out to 4000 feet (1219 m). The sensing gives nearness and general direction, never an exact spot."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Weapons and Equipment: it can use any kind of weapon, and wears little clothing or mega-damage armor except as a disguise in humanoid form. It mostly counts on what it was born with, its magic and its psionics."
  - "From the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules (p.156-159) the book defers to: a hatchling behaves like a child of four to seven and must settle on a definitive alignment at level three; it does not need to eat or drink; it can never take cybernetics or bionics, which its bio-regeneration pushes back out; and under 100 years old it cares little for wealth, though it is always drawn to magic items."
side_effects: "ADULT GHOST DRAGON (not playable; the class stores the hatchling). Attributes I.Q. 2D6+12, M.E. 2D6+14, M.A. 2D6+12, P.S. 3D6+20, P.P. 2D6+10, P.E. 2D6+10, P.B. 2D6+12, Spd 4D6+10 running and 1D6x10+100 flying or swimming. M.D.C. 4D6x100+1,300, +1D4x1,000 for an ancient (S.D.C. worlds: 3D6x10+40 Hit Points, 2D6x100+100 S.D.C., Natural A.R. 12). Horror Factor 14. P.P.E. 1D4x100. I.S.P. 3D4x10 + M.E., +5 per level; all Sensitive powers plus Empathic Transmission and Radiate Horror Factor. Eight physical attacks per melee round, or two by magic, or up to four breath weapon attacks. +3 on Perception Rolls, +2 initiative, +4 strike, +3 parry and dodge, +5 pull punch, +3 roll with impact, +7 vs Horror Factor, +2 on all other saves. Magic: one of Ocean Magic (30%), Wizard/Spell Invocations as a Ley Line Walker (30%) or Necromancy (40%), about 3D6+10 spells; never Warlock or Shifter. Life span 1D6x1,000+2,000 years, some reaching 10,000. NPC level: 2D4 for adults, 1D4 for hatchlings. Also called the Spectral Dragon or Sea Mist Dragon. Serpent Hunters hunt and kill this species, and other dragons - its own kind included - are rivals; Entities are its natural prey."
extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria printed 211-213 (cache p212-p214;
  printed 212 is full-page art). The figures on printed 211 and 213 were read
  off renders of both columns, not the text layer alone; the cache''s
  "1D4xl0" and "levelS" on p214 are 1D4x10 and level 8.

  Section heading: "Sea Dragons" (printed 208). A race, so no men_of_arms
  line is needed: the class states mdc_base.

  WHAT THE BOOK DEFERS TO RIFTS ULTIMATE EDITION, AND WHAT WAS REUSED.
  The entry says "Hatchling player characters start at level one" and twice
  sends the reader to Rifts Ultimate Edition p.156 for playing a dragon
  hatchling. Taken from the published dragon-hatchling-flame-wind class, not
  from this book:
  1. xp_table - the Rifts Ultimate Edition dragon ladder, copied from
     dragon-hatchling-flame-wind. This entry prints no ladder; the Leviathan
     in the same section (printed 209-210) says to use the Dragon Experience
     Table. Rifts Ultimate Edition''s Experience Tables (printed 295) head
     this ladder "Dragon Hatchling & Adult Dragon", and its hatchling
     section (printed 158) says to use the Dragon R.C.C. for level
     advancement.
  2. The spell-learning progression in the MAGIC restriction, and the last
     restriction line (alignment at level three, no need to eat, no
     cybernetics, money). This book prints only "know no spells at Level
     One ... can learn magic and use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical
     weapons and devices".
  3. The Magic Knowledge and Weapons and Equipment restriction lines, and
     "two spells per melee round, +1 to spell strength at level nine" in the
     MAGIC line. Rifts Ultimate Edition printed 158 prints all three in its
     general Dragon Hatchling section, as rules for every hatchling (the
     cache prints the spell strength figure as "+f"; it is +1).
  NOT reused: Rifts Ultimate Edition''s skill scheme (instinctive skills at
  98%, Secondary Skills, Special Areas of Interest). This entry prints its own
  "R.C.C. Skills (Hatchling)" list, which is what is stored.

  WHAT THE BOOK PRINTS AND WHAT WAS STORED.
  1. Skills: 11 named skills with a printed bonus; each base is the catalog
     base plus that bonus. "Underwater Navigation" is held as Navigation:
     Underwater, "Lore: Faerie & Creatures of Magic" as Lore: Faeries &
     Creatures of Magic, "Advanced Math" and "Basic Math" as Mathematics:
     Advanced and Mathematics: Basic, "Literate in Dragonese/Elven" as
     Literacy: Dragonese/Elven.
  2. "A total of four skill selections" from Communication, Rogue, Technical,
     Wilderness and W.P. is stored as a four-pick choice group in occ_skills
     with bonus 0. This entry''s list does not name Aquatic; the other three
     sea dragons'' lists do.
  3. "Magically understands and speaks all languages at 90%" is stored as
     Language: All (magical) at 90 with no per-level gain.
  4. Attacks: "Four physical or two by breath weapon attacks" is stored as
     attacks_base 4. The breath weapon''s own text says once per melee round;
     both are in prose. No by-magic figure is printed for this hatchling.
  5. "+1 on all other saving throws" is stored as +1 on each of the fourteen
     other d20 saves the sheet draws (the percentile coma/death save is left
     alone), following dragon-hatchling-asama-tatsu, and is also kept as a
     restriction line.
  6. Horror Factor 10 is stored in horror_factor.
  7. The S.D.C.-world figures (5D6+7 Hit Points, 2D6x10+25 S.D.C.) are stored
     in hit_points_base and sdc_base as the flame-wind model does; Natural
     A.R. 8 is prose.
  8. P.P.E. "1D6x10 + 10 points per level of experience" is read as 1D6x10 at
     level one, +10 per level.
  9. Psionics: five named powers granted, three picks from Sensitive, one pick
     at 4, 8, 12 and 16 (read as Sensitive: the sentence follows the Sensitive
     pick and names no other category), and Empathic Transmission at 8 as a
     one-name schedule entry. Sense Magic prints no I.S.P. cost; the catalog
     holds 3. "Commune with Spirits" is held as Commune with Spirit.
  10. Spd stores the running figure (2D6+7); double speed swimming or in Ghost
      Flight is prose.
  11. Adult and ancient figures are prose only (side_effects).
  12. Tags: four is the cap. `flyer` was left out in favour of `shapeshifter`;
      it flies only in Ghost Form.

  BOOK SLIPS.
  - Ghost Form, two statements. Printed 211 (introduction): four times a day.
    Printed 213 (the ability): as many times a day as it desires, no P.P.E.
    Both are in the ability''s description, unresolved.
  - "Turn invisible at will" (211) and "cannot turn invisible in Ghost Form"
    (213) are both recorded.
  - Printed 211 and 213: size, Mega-Damage and the natural abilities do not
    separate adult from hatchling. Stored once, as printed.
---

## Lore

A pale, serpentine dragon of the eastern kind: long body, short limbs, a crown
of horns, a beard and two trailing feelers, blank white eyes, and a fish-like
tail that ends in a fan of fur. It is a newcomer to Rifts Earth and a scavenger
by nature, drawn to shipwrecks, battlefields, Dead Pools and anywhere else the
dead collect.

Its name comes from the trick it is built around. It can shed its solid body
and drift as a see-through outline of itself, sliding through hulls and walls,
all but vanishing in fog or water until it is nearly on top of someone. The
price is that a ghost can touch nothing: to bite, cast or use its mind on
anyone it has to become solid again and stay that way for a moment.

A hatchling is a small, weak dragon by dragon standards, but it is a Master
Psychic from the egg, sees and speaks with spirits, and steals magic energy
with its breath.

## GM Notes

The book contradicts itself on how often the dragon may turn ethereal (four
times a day in the introduction, at will in the ability). Pick one before play.
At will makes the one-melee-round lockout the only brake on it.

The species leans hard toward selfish and evil alignments and is on the Serpent
Hunters'' list. A Ghost Dragon in a party of heroes is, by the book''s own
account, either a renegade or using them.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-hatchling-ghost');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-hatchling-ghost';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-dragon-hatchling-ghost-class.sql');
